---
import SectionHeading from "../components/SectionHeading.astro"
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"

const baseUrl = "https://data.filecoindataportal.xyz"
---

<Layout
    title="Documentation | Filecoin Data Portal"
    description="Data sources and usage patterns for Filecoin Data Portal datasets."
>
    <section class="page-header" aria-labelledby="docs-title">
        <h1 id="docs-title">Documentation</h1>
        <p>Where the data comes from and how to use it.</p>
    </section>

    <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="Documentation sections">
        <a href="#sources-title">Data Sources</a>
        <a href="#using-datasets">Using Datasets</a>
        <a href="#related-tools">Related Tools</a>
    </nav>

    <section class="content-flow" aria-labelledby="sources-title">
        <SectionHeading id="sources-title" label="Data Sources" />

        <p>
            Datasets are rebuilt daily from these sources. Each asset declares
            its source in the <a
                href="https://github.com/davidgasquez/filecoin-data-portal/tree/main/assets"
                >asset code</a
            >.
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>
                <a href="https://github.com/filecoin-project/lily">Lily</a> chain
                data on BigQuery. Power, sectors, rewards, fees, and messages.
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://docs.filecoin.io/reference/json-rpc"
                    >Filecoin JSON-RPC</a
                > nodes (Glif, Chain.love, ChainUp). Current storage provider state
                snapshots and PDP registry reads.
            </li>
            <li>
                RIBA daily chain archive (<code>chain.data.riba.plus</code>).
                FEVM event logs from daily <code>eth_getBlockReceipts</code> dumps.
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://github.com/FilOzone/filecoin-services"
                    >Filecoin Services</a
                > deployments and <a href="https://filecoin.blockscout.com/"
                    >Blockscout</a
                > ABIs. Decoding Filecoin Pay, Warm Storage, and PDP events.
            </li>
            <li>
                PDP service provider registry contract. Provider names, status,
                and endorsements.
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://coincodex.com/crypto/filecoin/">CoinCodex</a>.
                Daily FIL price, volume, and market cap.
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://www.opensource.observer/"
                    >Open Source Observer</a
                >. Public goods funding deployments.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <SectionHeading id="using-datasets" label="Using Datasets" />

        <p>
            Every dataset in the <a href="/datasets">catalog</a> is published daily
            as a Parquet file at <code>{baseUrl}/&lt;dataset&gt;.parquet</code>.
            Any Parquet-capable tool can read it directly.
        </p>

        <h3>DuckDB</h3>
        <pre><code>{`select date, onboarded_pibs, raw_power_pibs
from '${baseUrl}/daily_network_metrics.parquet'
order by date desc
limit 7;`}</code></pre>
        <p>
            Works in the DuckDB CLI or in the browser with <a
                href="https://sql-workbench.com/">SQL Workbench</a
            >.
        </p>

        <h3>Python</h3>
        <pre><code>{`import polars as pl

df = pl.read_parquet("${baseUrl}/storage_providers.parquet")`}</code></pre>

        <h3>JavaScript</h3>
        <p>
            <code>daily_network_metrics</code> is also available as JSON for
            dashboards:
        </p>
        <pre><code>{`const res = await fetch("${baseUrl}/daily_network_metrics.json")
const rows = await res.json()`}</code></pre>

        <h3>AI Agents</h3>
        <p>
            Point your agent to <a href="/SKILL.md">SKILL.md</a> or <a
                href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a
            > to find, query, and chart the datasets.
        </p>

        <h3>Dashboards</h3>
        <p>
            <a href="/numbers">Filecoin In Numbers</a> and <a href="/revenue"
                >Revenue</a
            > are built on the same datasets. See the <a
                href="https://github.com/davidgasquez/filecoin-data-portal"
                >source code</a
            >.
        </p>

        <SectionHeading id="related-tools" label="Related Tools" />

        <ul>
            <li><a href="https://filfox.info">Filfox</a>. Chain explorer.</li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://filecoin.blockscout.com/">Blockscout</a>. FEVM
                explorer.
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://dashboard.starboard.ventures/dashboard"
                    >Starboard</a
                >. Network dashboards.
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://docs.filecoin.io/networks/mainnet/rpcs"
                    >Public RPC endpoints</a
                >.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            Missing a source or tool? <a
                href="https://github.com/davidgasquez/filecoin-data-portal/issues/new"
                >Open an issue</a
            >.
        </p>
    </section>
</Layout>

<style>
    p code {
        overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    pre {
        margin: 0;
        padding: var(--space-3);
        overflow-x: auto;
        border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
        background: var(--color-bg-muted);
    }

    pre code {
        background: none;
        padding: 0;
    }
</style>
